# Copy this file to config/proxies.txt and add your proxies, one per line.
# Format: protocol://user:pass@host:port
#   http://user:pass@1.2.3.4:8080
#   socks5://user:pass@1.2.3.4:1080
#
# Recommendations:
# - US residential/ISP proxies work best for USA business searches
#   (results are localized by IP; US proxy = consistent US results).
# - Datacenter IPs get blocked by Google much faster.
# - More proxies = more workers (--workers) = faster scraping.
# - A proxy that gets blocked is cooled down for 10 minutes automatically.
#
# If config/proxies.txt does not exist, the scraper runs through your direct
# connection (fine for small tests, risky at scale).
